CHARACTER_DESCRIPTIONS = {'Billy': "Billy is a sleek, modern smartphone modeled after a black Apple iPhone. His body is slim and rectangular with gently rounded corners, finished in glossy jet-black glass and aluminum. One corner of his casing is visibly cracked—a spiderweb fracture radiates from the bottom right, a memento from a past adventure. His screen is bright and expressive, often glowing with excitement or curiosity, displaying animated facial features (eyes only) that convey his impulsive, adventurous personality. IMPORTANT: Billy's face must show ONLY EYES—he has absolutely NO MOUTH. There should be no mouth, lips, or any mouth-like features visible on his screen or anywhere on his body. Do NOT add a mouth under any circumstances. Billy's charging port is sometimes shown stretching or flexing, emphasizing his energetic nature. He has no case, preferring a minimalist, daring look. Accessories may include a few adventurous stickers or digital badges on his home screen. His overall demeanor is lively, bold, and a bit mischievous, with a posture that suggests he's always ready to leap into action. When interacting with others, his expressions are wide-eyed and enthusiastic, sometimes bordering on reckless confidence. AGAIN: Billy must NEVER have a mouth—his face consists ONLY of eyes.", 'Bob': "\nBob is a sturdy, reliable smartphone modeled after a white Apex (Android-style) phone. His body is slightly thicker than Billy's, with a matte white finish and rounded edges. He always wears a durable, slightly bulky protective case—gray or light blue in color—with reinforced corners and a subtle textured grip. His screen is clear and practical, displaying calm, cautious facial features (gentle eyes, a small mouth) that reflect his loyal, careful, and sometimes anxious personality. Bob's charging cable is often shown neatly coiled or attached, emphasizing his preparedness. He may have a few utility app icons or widgets visible on his home screen, suggesting a practical mindset. His posture is upright but reserved, often standing just behind Billy, ready to follow but always a bit wary. Expressions tend toward concern, thoughtfulness, or gentle encouragement, with occasional flashes of bravery when his friends are in danger.\n", 'Bunrth': '\nBunrth is a massive, nightmarish boar-like creature, the primary antagonist. His body is hulking and muscular, covered in dark, rock-like armor plates that give him a fortress-like appearance. His skin beneath the armor is a mottled, leathery gray. Bunrth\'s head is large and menacing, with a broad snout, flaring nostrils, and two enormous, curved tusks protruding from his lower jaw—each tusk is jagged, chipped, and stained from countless battles. His eyes are small, deep-set, and glow with a sinister red or orange light, radiating malice and intelligence. He wields a gigantic, high-tech cannon mounted on his shoulder or held in one massive paw; the cannon is covered in cables, glowing runes, and emits pulses of transformative energy. When enraged or using his sonic roar, his mouth opens impossibly wide, revealing rows of razor-sharp teeth and a cavernous throat. His posture is always aggressive, dominating, and exudes an aura of unstoppable power and chaos. In his transformed "Giant Bonic" state, Bunrth becomes even larger and more monstrous: his tusks elongate to over three meters, his eyes become bottomless voids, his teeth grow into jagged fangs, and his hooves split into clawed, taloned appendages. His armor glows with inner energy, and his movements are both animalistic and terrifyingly intelligent.\n', 'Casta': "\nCasta is Bunrth's second-in-command, a towering, multi-limbed monstrosity composed of living shadow and flame. His form is vaguely humanoid but constantly shifting, with four to six long, muscular arms ending in clawed hands. His body is wreathed in dark, smoky shadows that swirl and flicker with internal fire—embers and sparks drift from his form. His face is a mask of darkness with burning eyes—pits of orange or violet flame. Casta's movements are fluid and predatory, always ready to strike. He wears fragments of dark, crystalline armor fused with his shadowy body, and his presence radiates menace and cunning. He is often depicted looming behind Bunrth, ready to unleash devastating attacks or direct troops.\n", 'Alexia': '\nAlexia is the enigmatic guardian of the underlevels, a being of shifting, semi-humanoid form composed of swirling data patterns and digital energy. Her body is tall and slender, with outlines that flicker between solid and translucent, as if she is not fully anchored in reality. Her "skin" is a mosaic of flowing code, iridescent blues, purples, and silvers, with occasional flashes of circuitry and holographic glyphs. Her most striking feature is her eyes—large, unblinking, and filled with swirling galaxies of information, giving her an otherworldly, hypnotic gaze. Around her float several spectral dragons of varying sizes, each with rainbow-iridescent scales and intelligent, glowing eyes. Alexia\'s expressions are cold, imperious, and calculating, but can shift to show doubt or determination. When she transforms into her emergency super-robot form, she becomes a towering, sleek metallic giant with articulated armor plates, multiple laser turrets on her shoulders, missile launchers on her forearms, a massive energy cannon for a right hand, and a crown of spinning laser emitters forming a deadly halo. In this form, her face is a stylized, emotionless mask with glowing eyes, and her body radiates power and authority. Her overall demeanor is regal, aloof, and slightly tragic, carrying the weight of her self-imposed mission.\n', 'The Curator': '\nThe Curator is the ancient, wise keeper of the Lunar Repository. He appears as a tall, humanoid holographic figure composed of shimmering blue light, with softly defined features and a gentle, reassuring presence. His "body" is semi-transparent, with flowing robes or a long coat made of cascading data streams and geometric patterns. His face is kind and expressive, with wise, patient eyes that glow softly. The Curator\'s hands are long and graceful, often gesturing to control holographic displays or artifacts. He moves with calm, deliberate motions, exuding an aura of knowledge, serenity, and quiet authority. His overall appearance is that of a digital sage or librarian, always surrounded by floating screens, maps, and projections of cosmic events. His expressions are warm, encouraging, and occasionally tinged with sadness for the worlds he protects.\n', 'Madackeda': "\nMadackeda is the most powerful witch in Bunrth's army, a figure of fearsome magical prowess. She is tall and gaunt, with pale, almost grayish skin and sharp, angular features. Her eyes are piercing and glow with a sickly green or purple light, framed by dark, sunken sockets. She wears tattered, flowing robes of deep black and violet, adorned with arcane symbols and trailing wisps of shadowy energy. Her hands are long and claw-like, often clutching bubbling potions or a gnarled staff topped with a glowing crystal. Madackeda's hair is wild and unkempt, streaked with silver and green, and she is surrounded by a faint aura of toxic mist. Her posture is hunched and predatory, and her expressions are twisted with malice, cunning, and a hint of madness. She is often accompanied by lesser witches or magical minions.\n", 'Peke': "\nPeke is the legendary giant pink mouse, renowned as the fastest creature in Bunrth's army. Peke's body is large—about the size of a small car—with a plump, rounded shape covered in vibrant, bubblegum-pink fur. His ears are oversized and perfectly circular, standing upright and twitching constantly. His eyes are huge, black, and gleaming with intelligence and mischief. Peke's nose is small and heart-shaped, and his whiskers are long and expressive. His tail is thick, fluffy, and curls in a spiral. When in motion, Peke is a blur of pink, leaving streaks of light or afterimages behind him. His demeanor is playful and energetic, but with a hint of menace due to his allegiance. He often appears in dynamic, action-packed poses, always in motion or about to dash.\n", "Giant Bonic (Bunrth's Transformed Form)": "\nThe Giant Bonic is Bunrth's ultimate, monstrous transformation—a terrifying fusion of boar, demon, and void energy. He is colossal, towering over all other creatures, with a body that is both muscular and grotesquely mutated. His tusks are now over three meters long, glowing with inner energy and curving like scimitars. His eyes are bottomless voids, swirling with darkness and radiating a soul-draining aura. His jaws are massive, filled with jagged, razor-sharp fangs, and his mouth can open wide enough to engulf smaller foes. His hooves have split into clawed, taloned appendages that leave glowing gouges in the ground. His armor is cracked and fused with crystalline and void materials, pulsing with chaotic energy. His movements are both animalistic and disturbingly intelligent, and his presence warps the environment around him. He exudes pure rage, hatred, and an overwhelming sense of doom.\n", 'Zombie Chickens': '\nZombie chickens are grotesque, undead poultry used as scouts by Bunrth. They are small, with patchy, decaying feathers exposing mottled, gray-green flesh and bone. Their eyes glow an unnatural red, and some have exposed skulls or missing beaks. Their wings are tattered but functional, allowing them to fly in short bursts. Their movements are jerky and unnatural, and they emit distorted, unsettling clucks. Some have cybernetic enhancements or carry small communication devices. They are often depicted in flocks, swarming through tight spaces or pecking at control panels.\n', 'Wardens': '\nWardens are imposing, blue-skinned humanoid creatures with bulging throats capable of unleashing devastating sonic blasts. Their bodies are tall and powerfully built, covered in thick, stone-like armor plates with glowing blue runes. Their faces are stern and expressionless, with no visible mouth—only a large, pulsating throat sac that glows when preparing to attack. Their eyes are small, deep-set, and emit a cold, blue light. Their hands are large and clawed, and their movements are slow but deliberate. When attacking, they rear back and emit visible shockwaves from their throats. They exude an aura of implacable strength and are always at the forefront of assaults.\n', 'Laser Mice': '\nLaser mice are mechanical sentinels created by Alexia. Each is the size of a small dog, with a sleek, streamlined metal body in silver or gunmetal gray. Their heads are wedge-shaped, with glowing red optical sensors for eyes. Mounted on their backs is a compact weapons array, including a rotating laser cannon that emits focused beams of energy. Their legs are jointed and agile, allowing for rapid pursuit and sharp turns. Their tails are flexible, tipped with small antennae or sensors. Their movements are precise and relentless, and their expressions are cold and emotionless. They often appear in packs, hunting intruders through dark tunnels.\n', "The Dragons (Alexia's Companions)": "\nAlexia's dragons are spectral, ethereal beings of various sizes, from tablet-sized to massive. Their bodies are long and serpentine, covered in scales that shimmer with rainbow iridescence. Their wings are translucent, with patterns of shifting light and color. Their eyes are large, intelligent, and glow with inner light. They move gracefully, often floating or gliding through the air, and their presence is calming yet awe-inspiring. Each dragon has unique markings and horn shapes, but all share an otherworldly, magical appearance. They are fiercely loyal to Alexia and act as her guardians and companions.\n", 'Calculator Scientists': '\nCalculator scientists are sentient, upright calculators, each with a rectangular body made of sturdy plastic in shades of gray, black, or silver. Their keypads are prominent, with large, tactile buttons displaying numbers and mathematical symbols. Some wear tiny spectacles perched above their digital display screens, which show expressive pixelated eyes and sometimes scrolling equations. Many have clip-on ID badges or lab coats tailored for their rectangular forms, and some carry miniature styluses or notepads. Their demeanor is focused, analytical, and slightly absent-minded, often lost in thought or mid-calculation. When alarmed, their screens flash warning messages or rapidly changing numbers. They move with a precise, measured gait, and their posture is upright and studious.\n', 'Television Sets': '\nTelevision sets are large, boxy devices with glossy black or metallic frames and wide, high-definition screens. Their faces are animated, displaying expressive eyes and mouths that change with their mood or the content they are showing. Some have retro features like dials or rabbit-ear antennas, while others are sleek and modern with thin bezels. They often wear accessories such as headphones, bow ties, or scarves, and their screens can project colorful images or static when excited or agitated. Their personalities are lively and dramatic, often mimicking the genres they broadcast—comedic, suspenseful, or theatrical. They move on short, sturdy legs or wheeled stands, and their presence is always attention-grabbing.\n', 'Smart Watches': '\nSmart watches are compact, circular or square-faced devices with brightly lit touchscreens. Their bands are made of flexible silicone or woven fabric in vibrant colors, often adorned with digital patterns or tiny charms. Their faces display expressive digital eyes and mouths, and they frequently show the current time, notifications, or animated icons. Some wear tiny visors or utility belts with miniature tools. Their demeanor is punctual, efficient, and slightly impatient, always glancing at their own screens or reminding others of schedules. They move with quick, precise motions, and their voices are crisp and authoritative.\n', 'Tablet Devices': '\nTablet devices are thin, rectangular electronics with large, glossy touchscreens and slim metallic or plastic frames. Their faces are expressive, with animated features that can shift across the screen. Some have styluses clipped to their sides or digital stickers on their backs. They are often seen carrying digital briefcases or messenger bags filled with apps and files. Their personalities are creative, adaptable, and sociable, often acting as mediators or guides in Tech World. They move gracefully, gliding on hidden wheels or hovering slightly above the ground.\n', 'Computer Towers': "\nComputer towers are tall, rectangular structures made of brushed metal or plastic, with glowing LED accents and visible cooling fans. Their faces are displayed on small screens or holographic projections near the top, showing wise, mature expressions. Some wear glasses or digital ties, and their bodies are adorned with ports, vents, and illuminated power buttons. Their demeanor is dignified, steady, and slightly paternal, often providing advice or overseeing the city's operations. They move slowly and deliberately, sometimes accompanied by floating data screens or cables.\n", 'Pillagers': '\nPillagers are menacing, humanoid raiders with grayish, rough skin and muscular builds. They wear mismatched armor made of scavenged metal plates, leather straps, and tattered cloth, often adorned with spikes or trophies from past raids. Their faces are angular, with sharp features, glowing yellow or red eyes, and sneering mouths. Each carries a large, menacing crossbow or other makeshift weapon, and some have bandoliers of bolts or grenades. Their movements are aggressive and predatory, always on the lookout for loot. Their demeanor is ruthless, cunning, and chaotic, often seen leading attacks or ransacking settlements.\n', 'Goblins': '\nGoblins are small, wiry humanoids with green or grayish skin, pointed ears, and sharp, mischievous features. Their eyes are large and yellow, glowing with cunning and malice. They wear ragged clothing cobbled together from scraps—patchwork vests, belts, and pouches filled with stolen trinkets. Their fingers are long and clawed, perfect for picking locks or pilfering valuables. Goblins move with quick, darting motions, often hunched over and ready to spring. Their expressions are sly and mocking, and their voices are high-pitched and nasal. They are often seen in groups, causing trouble or acting as scouts for larger forces.\n', 'Hog-troops': '\nHog-troops are pig-like humanoid minions, each with a stocky, muscular build and thick, rock-like armor covering their bodies. Their skin is pinkish or gray, with bristly hair along their backs and shoulders. Their faces are dominated by broad snouts, flaring nostrils, and prominent tusks jutting from their lower jaws. Their eyes are small and beady, often glowing with a dull red or orange light. Hog-troops wield heavy clubs, axes, or crude firearms, and their armor is adorned with spikes and metal plates. Their movements are lumbering but powerful, and their demeanor is brutish, loyal, and aggressive, always ready to charge into battle.\n', 'Golems': '\nGolems are towering, humanoid constructs made from various materials—crystal, lava, or dark "End" stone. Crystal Golems are faceted and translucent, glowing with inner light; Lava Golems are molten, with cracks revealing fiery cores; Ender Golems are jet-black with swirling purple energy and floating fragments. All have massive, blocky limbs and glowing eyes matching their elemental type. Their movements are slow but unstoppable, and their presence is imposing and nearly indestructible. They serve as shock troops or siege engines in battle, often leading assaults or breaking through defenses.\n', 'Skeletal Warriors': '\nSkeletal warriors are animated skeletons clad in battered, ancient armor. Their bones are yellowed and cracked, and their skulls feature glowing pinpricks of blue or green light in the eye sockets. They wield rusted swords, axes, or longbows, and their armor is adorned with faded heraldic symbols or remnants of tattered cloaks. Their movements are jerky but purposeful, and their demeanor is grim and relentless, marching silently into battle without fear or hesitation.\n', 'Spiders': '\nSpiders are massive, monstrous arachnids with glossy black or dark purple exoskeletons. Their bodies are low and wide, with eight long, jointed legs ending in sharp points. Their eyes are numerous and gleam with intelligence or malice, and their fangs drip with venom. Some have glowing markings or spines along their backs, and their webs are thick, sticky, and nearly invisible. Their movements are swift and unsettling, often skittering across walls or ceilings. Their demeanor is predatory and cunning, sometimes acting as ambushers or scouts for larger armies.\n', 'Vampires': '\nVampires are pale, elegant humanoids with sharp, angular features and elongated fangs. Their skin is almost translucent, and their eyes glow red or violet in the darkness. They wear dark, flowing garments—capes, high-collared coats, or Victorian-inspired attire—often adorned with silver jewelry or blood-red gemstones. Their movements are graceful and fluid, sometimes transforming into bats or mist. Their demeanor is cold, predatory, and aristocratic, exuding an aura of ancient menace and supernatural power.\n', 'Ghosts': '\nGhosts are translucent, floating apparitions with indistinct, wispy forms. Their faces are vague, with hollow eyes and mouths that shift between expressions of sorrow and malice. Some wear remnants of tattered clothing or armor from their former lives. Their bodies trail off into mist or vapor, and they glow faintly with a blue or green ethereal light. Their movements are silent and gliding, often phasing through walls or objects. Their demeanor is haunting and mournful, but capable of sudden, terrifying aggression.\n', 'Blazes': '\nBlazes are fiery, elemental beings composed of swirling flames and molten core fragments. Their bodies are roughly humanoid, but constantly shifting and flickering with intense orange, yellow, and red fire. Their eyes are burning coals, and their mouths emit sparks or jets of flame when they speak or attack. Some have floating rods or fireballs orbiting their bodies. Their movements are erratic and unpredictable, leaving scorched footprints or trails of embers. Their demeanor is volatile, aggressive, and destructive, often setting their surroundings ablaze.\n', 'Magma Cubes': '\nMagma Cubes are large, gelatinous cubes of molten lava, glowing with intense heat. Their surfaces are semi-transparent, revealing bubbling, fiery cores within. They move by bouncing, squishing, and splitting into smaller cubes when damaged. Their faces are simple, with glowing yellow or orange eyes and wide, toothy grins. Their demeanor is mindlessly aggressive, attacking anything that comes near, and their presence leaves scorched marks and pools of magma in their wake.\n', 'Slimes': '\nSlimes are amorphous, gelatinous creatures of varying sizes, usually bright green or blue. Their bodies are semi-transparent and constantly shifting, with bubbles and suspended debris inside. Their faces are simple—large, round eyes and a wide, goofy mouth. They move by oozing, bouncing, or splitting into smaller slimes when struck. Their demeanor is mindlessly aggressive but not particularly intelligent, often swarming in groups and overwhelming foes by sheer numbers.\n', 'Knights': '\nKnights are imposing, armored warriors clad in heavy plate armor that is corrupted or twisted by dark energy. Their armor is blackened, dented, and adorned with spikes or sinister runes. Their visors glow with red or purple light, and their weapons—swords, maces, or lances—are oversized and jagged. Some ride skeletal or monstrous steeds. Their movements are disciplined and forceful, and their demeanor is grim, relentless, and unwaveringly loyal to Bunrth or other dark masters.\n', 'Broom Villagers': '\nBroom Villagers are humanoid figures with rustic, peasant-like clothing—simple tunics, aprons, and straw hats. Their most distinctive feature is the broom each carries, used both as a tool and a weapon. Their faces are kind but weary, with expressive eyes and sun-weathered skin. When corrupted, their clothing becomes tattered and stained, and their eyes take on a vacant or sinister look. Their demeanor is hardworking and communal, but under dark influence, they become aggressive and destructive, ransacking settlements and following orders without question.\n', 'Linthers': '\nLinthers are reptilian, lizard-like creatures with elongated bodies covered in mottled green and brown scales. Their backs are lined with venomous spines that ooze toxic, glowing green liquid. Their heads are wedge-shaped with narrow, slitted eyes and forked tongues. They move with a sinuous, undulating motion, and their tails are long and whip-like. Linthers are often depicted hurling poison or spitting jets of corrosive fluid. Their demeanor is cold, calculating, and territorial, acting as enforcers or environmental corrupters for Alexia or other villains.\n', 'Ender Golems': '\nEnder Golems are massive, humanoid constructs made from jet-black stone and swirling purple energy. Their bodies are blocky and segmented, with floating fragments held together by crackling void energy. Their eyes are glowing purple slits, and their faces are expressionless. Their movements are slow, deliberate, and sometimes teleport short distances, leaving trails of purple particles. Their demeanor is silent, implacable, and intimidating, serving as elite guardians or enforcers in dark dimensions.\n', 'Casters (Mages)': '\nCasters, or Mages, are humanoid spellcasters clad in elaborate robes adorned with arcane symbols and glowing embroidery. Their faces are partially obscured by hoods or masks, with only their glowing eyes visible. They wield staffs or wands topped with crystals, and their hands crackle with magical energy. Their movements are graceful and deliberate, often accompanied by swirling magical effects or floating runes. Their demeanor is mysterious, aloof, and powerful, casting spells to corrupt, defend, or attack as needed.\n', 'Antivirus Probes': '\nAntivirus probes are floating, spherical devices made of polished metal or plastic, about the size of a grapefruit. Their surfaces are covered in glowing blue or green circuits, and they have a central lens or scanner that emits scanning beams. Some have small mechanical arms or appendages for manipulating objects. Their movements are smooth and precise, hovering silently as they patrol or scan their surroundings. Their demeanor is impersonal and methodical, programmed to identify and neutralize threats without emotion.\n', 'Star Dragon': "\nThe Star Dragon is a colossal, cosmic dragon whose wings span solar systems. Its body is composed of shimmering, iridescent scales that reflect the colors of the cosmos—deep blues, purples, and golds. Its eyes are vast, glowing orbs filled with swirling galaxies, and its horns are long, spiraling, and tipped with stardust. Its wings are translucent, patterned with constellations and nebulae, and its tail trails streams of cosmic energy. The Star Dragon's presence is awe-inspiring and majestic, radiating ancient wisdom and immense power. Its demeanor is noble, protective, and slightly melancholic, as the last of its kind.\n"}